  "notes": ["The original near-only collision walk produces support and saves the local anchor on the same allocated foreign plane. No support flag, pointer or anchor is seeded by the host.","Declared changes affect the original joint matrix read through the plane cell. Both original queries return the reprojected Y. The surface query returns the saved normal, even after the original shape rebuild publishes the rotated plane normal.","The normal Sasuke installer supplies the actor configuration. The original landing helper follows an upward support height, keeps X/Z, refuses a lowered support while above it, and leaves the already allocated capsule center unchanged.","The original reset copies current support to the previous flag and clears current support. The plane pointer and anchor remain, but neither query uses them; the declared empty floor supplies the fallback.","Each case is a fresh bounded fork after the original near contact. There is no full actor tick, platform driver, lateral carrying, floor integration, live stage, hardware or native gameplay qualification."],
